# <type>(<scope>): <description>
# │       │             │
# │       │             └─> Summary in present tense. Not capitalized. No period at the end.
# │       │
# │       └─> Scope: cli|app|domain|config|workflow|shell|runner|rules|baseline|report|fixtures|action|release|deps|docs|tooling (optional)
# │
# └─> Type: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore

# Body (optional): Explain *what* and *why* vs. *how*


# Footer (optional): Reference issues, breaking changes
# Examples:
#   Fixes #123
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conventional Commits v1.0.0 - https://conventionalcommits.org
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Types:
#   feat:     A new feature (MINOR version bump)
#   fix:      A bug fix (PATCH version bump)
#   docs:     Documentation only changes
#   style:    Formatting only (no code change)
#   refactor: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf:     Performance improvement
#   test:     Adding or correcting tests or fixtures
#   build:    Changes to the build system, Taskfile, goreleaser or dependencies
#   ci:       Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
#   chore:    Other changes that don't modify src or test files
#
# Breaking Changes:
#   Add ! after type/scope: feat!: or feat(baseline)!:
#   Or add footer: BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
#   Rule IDs, the baseline format and the JSON schema are public contracts.
#
# Examples:
#   feat(shell): peel transparent wrappers before matching tools
#   fix(workflow): report block-scalar run lines one line below the key
#   test(fixtures): add includes-nested fixture
#   feat(baseline)!: rename the workflows key
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
